The ogive of the daily sales, in rupees, of $80$ imagined street-food carts passes through $(100, 0)$, $(150, 5)$, $(200, 12)$, $(250, 28)$, $(300, 48)$, $(350, 72)$ and $(400, 80)$. Read from it (accept $\pm 1$ on counts and $\pm 5$ on sales):

(a) the number of carts with sales below $275$;

(b) the number of carts with sales above $325$;

(c) the least sales needed to be among the best $20$ carts, and the number of carts with sales between $250$ and $325$.
